// Deal or Force - what a long war does to the countries fighting it (WarWeariness.cs).
//
// Granted every week to every country in a war older than PeaceWearinessAfterDays (two years),
// and the heavier one once it is older than AiWearyDays (four); each lapses a fortnight after the
// war ends. The same grammar as 00_modifiers.json.
//
// ─── The nuclear shadow ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// Granted IN ADDITION to the long-war weight when BOTH sides of a war hold the
// deterrent (Deterrence.Briskmanship > 0). It is the home-front half of the Cuba
// rule (AiPeaceOutcomes.WriteDecisiveSettlement): the same pressure that ends such
// wars in limited terms is what every household under the shadow lives with.
// A mod without `common/deterrence` data never triggers this — the spirit is
// unreachable and harmless in an ordinary world.
{
  "long_war": {
    "name": "A long war",
    "description": "The war is in its third year. The funerals have stopped being news, and so have the victories.",
    "days": 14,
    "positive": false,
    "modifiers": {
      "war_support_weekly": -0.003,
      "stability_weekly": -0.0012,
      "output": -0.02
    }
  },
